2. **May `memory_index.py` gain `--check --json`?** If yes, one contract with ids. If no, I parse stderr and pin it with tests (brittle) or narrow C3 and own the format checks (duplicates a checker).
3. **Which snapshot?** If the warning is HEAD-only, uncommitted memory is not warned; if working-tree, K6 can't be judged until staged. My default: warning HEAD, report `--rev`/`--all`; both print the snapshot.
